      "text": "The history of art and architecture is not primarily a history of taste — it is a history of technical innovation, intellectual programs, and responses to material and social conditions. Every major shift corresponds to something: a new engineering method, a new theory of vision, a political commission, a response to industrialization, a collapse of shared assumptions."
    },
